<div class="table-responsive">
	<TableTemplate TItem="ConstellationDTO" Items="Items" HeaderCSS="table table-sm table-striped align-middle">
		<TableHeader>
			<th>Order</th>
			<th>Month</th>
			<th>Sign</th>
			@* <th>Mazzarah</th> *@
			<th class="text-center">Hebrew</th>
			<th>Key Idea</th>
			<th>Meaning</th>
			<th>Main Stars</th>

			@* <th>Verses</th> *@
		</TableHeader>
		<RowTemplate>
			<td>@context.CircleOrder - @context.MonthOrder </td>
			<td>@context.Month</td>
			<td class="fw-bold">@context.Sign</td>
			@* <td>@context.Mazzarah</td> *@
			<td>
				<div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-baseline">
					<span class="fst-italic">@context.HebrewTransliteration</span>
					<span dir="rtl">@context.HebrewWord</span>
				</div>
			</td>

			<td>@context.KeyIdea</td>
			<td>@context.Meaning</td>
			<td>@context.MainStars</td>
	@* 	<td>@context.Verses</td>*@
		</RowTemplate>
	</TableTemplate>
</div>

<h5>Additional Notes on Common Christian Mazzaroth Teaching</h5>
<ul>
	<li><strong>Starting point</strong>: Most of these writers begin the circle with <strong>Virgo</strong> (the Seed of the woman, <a href="https://www.blueletterbible.org/kjv/gen/3/15/" target="_blank">Gen 3:15</a>) rather than Aries, so the story runs from the promise to the final triumph.</li>
	<li><strong>Orion</strong> is often treated as a major decan of Taurus — “the Coming of the Branch,” with Betelgeuse, Rigel (“the foot that crushes”), and Bellatrix.</li>
	<li><strong>Draco</strong> is frequently linked to the serpent of <a href="https://www.blueletterbible.org/kjv/gen/3/1/" target="_blank">Genesis 3</a> and <a href="https://www.blueletterbible.org/kjv/rev/12/1/" target="_blank">Revelation 12</a>.</li>
	<li>These readings are <strong>interpretive tradition</strong>, not direct biblical statements of the constellation meanings. The Bible itself only names a few of the groups (Kimah, Kesil, Ash/Ayish, Mazzaroth).</li>
</ul>

@code {
	[Parameter, EditorRequired] public IReadOnlyList<ConstellationDTO> Items { get; set; } = [];
}
